ion in central bank balance sheet management that warrants monitoring. India's fundamental structural paradox is unchanged and deepening: maximum diplomatic deployment (five-nation tour completed, US relationship repair, Nordic institutionalization, Quad FM upcoming) alongside maximum economic stress (RBI forex defense, rupee pressure, $100B deficit gap warning); maximum domestic political consolidation (208 WB seats, tribal coalition management, Adani legal clearance) alongside maximum civilizational rebranding intensity (Janjati Mahakumbh, Smart Border Demography Mission); and a BRICS chairship that remains structurally constrained by the same Iran/UAE conflict that the Rubio visit may be resolving via a US-Iran deal.",
